   "notes": "Street front of Corpus's Bene't Hostel block (5 Bene't St): buff/cream render, two sash bays per upper floor. Blue-grey painted timber shopfront ('cambridge contemporary crafts' in lower-case lettering on the fascia) with a projecting moulded cornice and multi-pane display windows. There is a recessed doorway with a white door at the east end. I am not sure the 2nd-floor windows match the 1st-floor ones exactly: they were only partly in frame."
